# DB / Prisma / RLS (full text: docs/09_Codebase/08_Patterns.md §1, §3)
- Schema source = `supabase/migrations/*.sql`. **`prisma db push` is forbidden** (MIG-001). After a migration: local reset + `pnpm db:generate`.
- Assign the migration number at implementation time; never rename an applied migration (MIG-002).
- IDs: `uuid_generate_v7()` (RULE-11). Every UUID field in Prisma has `@db.Uuid` (RULE-05). Enum change order: RULE-15.
- A column used by an RLS policy cannot change type — plan migrations accordingly.
- New tenant table: ENABLE + FORCE RLS + policy `TO app_user` + GRANT; for camp/core tables `SELECT camp_apply_tenant_rls('<table>');` (RULE-12).
- Tenant data always inside `inTenantTx(prisma, tenantId, tx => …)`; `set_config('app.tenant_id', …, true)`, never `SET LOCAL` (RULE-03/04).
- `SYSTEM_DATABASE_URL` only for system jobs.
- Prisma reads `apps/core-kernel/.env` (not the root `.env`).
